# Lazy-loaded images must survive

A WordPress-style lazy loader: a data: placeholder in src, the real URL in data-src, and a noscript fallback beside it.

![from data-src](https://example.com/uploads/data-src.jpg)

A rocket-loader style data-lazy-src, behind an http spacer:

![from data-lazy-src](https://cdn.example.com/lazy-src.png)

Only a responsive srcset, CDN commas and all; the widest candidate wins:

![from srcset](https://cdn.example.com/w_1200,h_900/srcset.jpg)

A placeholder whose only real source is the noscript fallback:

![from noscript](https://cdn.example.com/noscript.webp)

And an ordinary image, untouched: ![plain](https://cdn.example.com/plain.png)
